IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `tulrca-types`
IMPORT `tulrca-periods`

-- Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992 (UK) — GOAL 1:
-- UNION MEMBERSHIP AND ACTIVITIES (ss 146-161).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1992-52.txt.
-- The worker asks: "I was treated badly, or dismissed, because of my union
-- membership or activities (or for not joining). Am I protected; by when
-- must I complain; can I get interim relief; what is the least basic award?"

§ `Goal 1 — union membership and activities`

-- s 146(1)-(3) and 152(1)-(3) share the protected reasons; (b) and (ba) only
-- "at an appropriate time".
@ref ss 146(1)-(3), 152(1)-(3)
GIVEN u IS A `Union case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the reason is a protected one for` u IF
    CONSIDER u's `the reason`
    WHEN `membership of an independent trade union`  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `taking part in independent union activities` THEN u's `at an appropriate time`
    WHEN `making use of union services`              THEN u's `at an appropriate time`
    WHEN `refusing an unlawful inducement`           THEN TRUE
    WHEN `not being a member`                        THEN TRUE
    WHEN `refusing payments in lieu of membership`   THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 146(1), (5A): a worker's right not to suffer a detriment; for an
-- employee, not where the detriment is dismissal. A worker who is not an
-- employee keeps s 146 when the engagement is ended (changed after the
-- independent pass).
-- s 152(1): an employee's dismissal for a protected reason is unfair.
-- s 153: selection for redundancy for such a reason, where others similarly
-- placed were not dismissed, is unfair.
@ref ss 146(1), (5A), 152(1), 153
@export Am I protected under the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992 (UK)? A worker subjected to a detriment by the employer for the sole or main purpose of preventing, deterring or penalising union membership, union activities or use of union services at an appropriate time, of compelling membership, or because of a refusal of an unlawful inducement or of payments in lieu of membership (s 146); or an employee dismissed (s 152), or selected for redundancy while others similarly placed were kept on (s 153), for such a reason — whose dismissal is then automatically unfair. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN u IS A `Union case`  @desc The reason found, whether activities were at an appropriate time, whether I am an employee, and what was done to me
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I am protected under the union provisions` u IF
        `the reason is a protected one for` u
    AND CONSIDER u's `the treatment`
        WHEN `a detriment short of dismissal` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `dismissal`                      THEN TRUE
        WHEN `selection for redundancy`       THEN (NOT (u's `an employee`)) OR u's `others similarly placed were not dismissed`

-- s 146(5A): the complaint is under s 146 unless the worker is an employee
-- and the detriment amounts to dismissal.
@ref s 146(5A)
GIVEN u IS A `Union case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the complaint is under s 146 for` u IF
        u's `the treatment` EQUALS `a detriment short of dismissal`
    OR  NOT (u's `an employee`)

-- s 154: the two-year qualifying period and the upper age limit do not apply
-- to a dismissal unfair by virtue of s 152 or 153.
@ref s 154
GIVEN u IS A `Union case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the qualifying period is disapplied for` u IF
        `I am protected under the union provisions` u
    AND NOT (`the complaint is under s 146 for` u)

-- s 147(1)(a): "before the end of the period of three months beginning with
-- the date of the act or failure ... or ... the last of them", extended by
-- s 292A (s 147(4)). Only for a s 146 complaint; a dismissal complaint is
-- made under the Employment Rights Act 1996.
@ref s 147(1)(a), (4), 292A
@export The last day to present a complaint of a detriment on union grounds under s 147 of the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992 (UK): the end of the three months beginning with the act (or the last of a series), extended for ACAS early conciliation by s 292A. NOTHING for an employee's dismissal, whose time limit is in the Employment Rights Act 1996; a worker who is not an employee complains of the ending of the engagement under s 146. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN u IS A `Union case`  @desc The act, the treatment, and any early conciliation
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day to complain of the detriment for` u MEANS
    IF `the complaint is under s 146 for` u
    THEN JUST (`the last day of` 3 `months beginning with` (u's `act on`) `extended by` (u's `early conciliation`))
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 161(1)-(2): interim relief for a dismissal alleged unfair by virtue of
-- s 152, "before the end of the period of seven days immediately following
-- the effective date of termination (whether before, on or after that
-- date)".
@ref s 161(1)-(2)
@export The last day to apply for interim relief under s 161 of the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992 (UK): seven days after the effective date of termination. NOTHING unless the complaint is of an employee's dismissal under s 152. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN u IS A `Union case`  @desc The treatment and the effective date of termination
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day to apply for interim relief for` u MEANS
    IF u's `the treatment` EQUALS `dismissal` AND u's `an employee`
    THEN CONSIDER u's `effective date of termination`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST t  THEN JUST (`the day` 7 `days after` t)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 161(3): for reasons under s 152(1)(a), (b), (ba), or (bb) other than an
-- offer under s 145A(1)(d), a union certificate must also be presented in
-- the same period.
@ref s 161(3)
GIVEN u IS A `Union case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a union certificate is needed for` u IF
    CONSIDER u's `the reason`
    WHEN `membership of an independent trade union`  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `taking part in independent union activities` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `making use of union services`              THEN TRUE
    WHEN `refusing an unlawful inducement`           THEN NOT (u's `the offer was under s 145A(1)(d)`)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN m IS A MAYBE DATE, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `presented on` m `by` d IF
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST x  THEN x AT MOST d

@ref s 161(1)-(3)
@export Can the tribunal entertain my application for interim relief under s 161 of the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992 (UK)? It must be presented within seven days after the effective date of termination (it may be before), and, where the reason relied on is union membership, activities or services, or an unlawful inducement other than under s 145A(1)(d), a signed union certificate must be presented in that time too. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN u IS A `Union case`  @desc The reason, the dismissal, and the days the application and any certificate were presented
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `my interim relief application is in time for` u IF
    CONSIDER `the last day to apply for interim relief for` u
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST last THEN
            `presented on` (u's `interim relief applied for on`) `by` last
        AND (    NOT (`a union certificate is needed for` u)
             OR `presented on` (u's `union certificate presented on`) `by` last)

-- s 156(1): for a dismissal unfair by virtue of s 152(1) or 153, the basic
-- award before any reduction under s 122 of the 1996 Act is not less than
-- £9,157.
@ref s 156(1)
@export The basic award, before reductions, for a dismissal on union grounds under s 156(1) of the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992 (UK): the award under the Employment Rights Act 1996, but not less than £9,157 where the dismissal is unfair by virtue of s 152(1) or 153. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN u IS A `Union case`  @desc The case and the basic award worked out under the Employment Rights Act 1996
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the basic award before reductions for` u MEANS
    IF `the qualifying period is disapplied for` u AND (u's `basic award before reductions`) LESS THAN 9157
    THEN 9157
    ELSE u's `basic award before reductions`
